// {"files":[{"path":"\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\OneDrive\\github-repos\\infra-pilot\\wiki\\03-Configuration.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":46,"oldLines":4,"newStart":46,"newLines":16,"lines":[" - `FEDERATION_API_TOKEN` protects the orchestrator `/api/` route group when configured. Do not expose it to browsers."," - The Discord service has access to `/var/run/docker.sock` in Compose; restrict it to trusted hosts and administrators."," ","-See [`.env.example`](../.env.example) and the service-level `.env.example` files for exact defaults.","+See [`.env.example`](../.env.example) and the service-level `.env.example` files for exact defaults.","+","+## Feature flags","+","+- The panel owns flags (`feature_flags` + `feature_flag_rules` tables).","+  Admins manage them at `/feature-flags` in the UI; every change is audit-logged.","+- Consumers (orchestrator `feature_flags.py`, CLI `ipilot flags`, Discord","+  `feature-flags.js`) poll `GET /api/feature-flags/evaluate` every 30 s.","+  Set `FEATURE_FLAGS_ENABLED=true` to opt in; default is `false` (code defaults apply).","+- Kill switch: `POST /api/feature-flags/:key/kill` (or the Kill button, or","+  `ipilot flags kill <key>`) disables a flag in all environments at once.","+- Incident escape hatch: `FEATURE_FLAG_<KEY>=true|false` env var beats the","+  remote value in every consumer; the React app also honours `VITE_FEATURE_FLAG_<KEY>`."]}]}]}
